# Third-party Omarchy shell plugins. Installed by install.sh into
# ~/.config/omarchy/plugins/<id>/. Same contract as:
#   omarchy plugin add <url> [--enable]
# Apply clones and (with --enable) writes shell.json. It does not call the
# live omarchy-plugin-add CLI, which needs a running omarchy-shell.
#
# --enable is a seed, not a setting. It is honoured on the apply that clones
# the plugin and never again, because `omarchy plugin disable` records itself
# only as absence from shell.json and an enable on every apply would overturn
# it every update. Switch one back on with `omarchy plugin enable <id>`.
#
# Deleting a row here stops nothing that is already installed. To be rid of a
# plugin: drop the row, then `omarchy plugin remove <id>`.
#
# Grok usage is a stopgap fork: upstream dougfour/omarchy-grok-usage lost its
# Grok tab when omarchy stopped passing __sourceDir, and the fixes sit in its
# open PRs #2 and #3. The fork is upstream plus those two merges, nothing else.
# The username in its URL is an agreed exception to AGENTS.md "No names".
# Return to https://github.com/dougfour/omarchy-grok-usage.git once both land.
# Either way, an existing checkout keeps its origin -- apply sees the id already
# there and leaves it -- so switch one by hand:
#   git -C ~/.config/omarchy/plugins/io.github.dougfour.grok-usage remote set-url origin <url>
#   omarchy plugin update io.github.dougfour.grok-usage --yes && omarchy restart shell
https://github.com/dieuwedeboer/omarchy-grok-usage.git --enable
